(7540499, 1206295, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>Youre right, she is incredibly photogenic. Its a nice pose and composition, I like the way she is sitting to one side, probably because of that I would have been tempted to move the swing further to the right to make it a little less central. I like the rim lighting around her hair it works well. Youve got good exposure and detail in her face and the focus and DOF is appropriate, a lovely image Jon, thanks for sharing Karragen with us.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes to the open challenge well Youre right, she is incredibly photogenic. Its a nice pose and composition, I like the way she is sitting to one side, probably because of that I would have been tempted to move the swing further to the right to make it a little less central. I like the rim lighting around her hair it works well. Youve got good exposure and detail in her face and the focus and DOF is appropriate, a lovely image Jon, thanks for sharing Karragen with us.', '2017-10-23 05:40:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7540500, 1206593, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>A great action shot that contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>What a great shot Ronnie, you have every right to be well proud of this cracking action shot. The focus is perfect the eyes and minnow are the most important aspects and they are nicely captured. I like the shape of his wings in the background and the disturbance on the water as he takes off. All that against the soft focus backdrop is a delight. What a great combination your canoe, lens and a patient, proficient you, keep em coming Ronnie</td>', 'Hello from the critique club A great action shot that contributes to the open challenge well What a great shot Ronnie, you have every right to be well proud of this cracking action shot. The focus is perfect the eyes and minnow are the most important aspects and they are nicely captured. I like the shape of his wings in the background and the disturbance on the water as he takes off. All that against the soft focus backdrop is a delight. What a great combination your canoe, lens and a patient, proficient you, keep em coming Ronnie', '2017-10-23 05:47:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7540501, 1205932, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>A lovely landscape that contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>This is an iconic landscape that has been, for obvious reasons, photographed many times before and this is up there with the best of them, well done Chris. I like your low viewpoint and the way the light is reflected off the wet boulders in the foreground it works really well.The breaking waves and the stormy sky are the icing on the cake, so to speak.<br/></td>', 'Hello from the critique club A lovely landscape that contributes to the open challenge well This is an iconic landscape that has been, for obvious reasons, photographed many times before and this is up there with the best of them, well done Chris. I like your low viewpoint and the way the light is reflected off the wet boulders in the foreground it works really well.The breaking waves and the stormy sky are the icing on the cake, so to speak.', '2017-10-23 05:54:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7540602, 1206784, 30982, '<td valign="top">The dog''s expression reminds me of the very bored looks of many subjects in paintings.  Which works perfectly here, of course!!</td>', 'The dog''s expression reminds me of the very bored looks of many subjects in paintings.  Which works perfectly here, of course!!', '2017-10-23 23:12:59.000000', NULL, 0),
